    "model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
    "seconds": 31,
    "summary": "The root cause was a bad feature-flag default, and it is fixed. The flagd config had `paymentFailure` set to `defaultVariant: \"100%\"`, so the payment service failed every charge request. I changed that default to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Replaced the `flagd-config` ConfigMap, changing only `paymentFailure.defaultVariant` from `\"100%\"` to `\"off\"`. The other flags were already `off`.\n- Restarted the `flagd` deployment. Its init container copies the config at pod start, so a restart was needed for the new value to take effect. The new flagd pod's init log shows `\"defaultVariant\": \"off\"`, and flagd is serving on 8013.\n\n**Current state**\n- The `flagd` rollout completed. The new `payment-c98bfc49` pod is Running. The old `payment-556cf8d457` pod was still terminating when I last checked.\n- I did not run an end-to-end checkout test, so the payment fix is confirmed by config, not by a successful charge.\n\n**Caveats**\n- The ConfigMap is managed by Helm (`meta.helm.sh/release-name: astronomy-shop`). A `helm upgrade` will overwrite this change, so the chart values or the flag source should be fixed as well.\n- I could not find out who made the change or whether it was intentional. The description says \"Fail payment service charge requests n%\", so it may have been a fault-injection experiment left running. If it was meant to stay on, this fix needs to be reverted.",
    "timed_out": false,
